---
import BrowserSupport from "../components/BrowserSupport.astro";
import PNotes from "../components/PNotes.astro";
---

<p-slide>
  <h3 class="main-gradient">Readable text, computed</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      🎨 <span>Change the </span>
      <span class="main-sub-gradient">background token</span>
    </li>
    <li p-fragment p-effect="from right">
      🔤 <span>The text color </span>
      <span class="main-sub-gradient">follows</span>
      <span> - black or white</span>
    </li>
    <li p-fragment p-effect="from left">
      👀 <span>A starting point, </span>
      <span class="main-sub-gradient">not a contrast audit</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <PNotes>
    <p>
      One more color function, newly Baseline (April 2026): contrast-color().
      Give it a color, it returns white or black - whichever contrasts more.
    </p>
    <p>
      Be honest on the third bullet: it only returns white or black, and it
      targets WCAG AA. On mid-tone backgrounds (MDN's example: #2277d3) neither
      is readable for small text. Use it with light or dark tokens - the
      designer still checks the palette.
    </p>
  </PNotes>
</p-slide>

<p-slide>
  <h5 style="margin-block-end: 1em" class="center">
    <span class="main-gradient">contrast-color()</span> - one token, readable
    text 🔤
  </h5>
  <pre class="small-line" data-label-file="button.css">
    <code style="font-size: 0.7em" is:raw class="language-scss">
    button {
        background: var(--accent);
        /* white or black - whichever contrasts more */
        color: contrast-color(var(--accent));
    }</code>
  </pre>

  <PNotes>
    <p>
      Same --accent token as the card. Change it at runtime and the button text
      flips between black and white by itself.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before: a Sass function picking the text color at build time, or a second
      token to keep in sync by hand.
    </p>
  </PNotes>
</p-slide>

<BrowserSupport
  feature="contrast-color()"
  chrome="147"
  firefox="146"
  safari="26"
  status="Baseline 2026 - newly available"
/>
